================================================================================
WAYBAR CORE MODULES & PROPERTIES REFERENCE GUIDE
================================================================================

This document covers the core modules provided by Waybar and their most common 
and important properties. Waybar configuration uses JSONC format.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. GLOBAL MODULE PROPERTIES (Applies to almost all modules)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- format            : (string) Defines the text/layout to display. Supports Pango 
                      markup and placeholder tokens specific to the module.
- rotate            : (integer) Rotate the module by 0, 90, 180, or 270 degrees.
- max-length        : (integer) The maximum length of the module text in characters.
- min-length        : (integer) The minimum length of the module text in characters.
- align             : (float) Alignment of the text within the module (0.0 to 1.0).
- tooltip           : (bool) Enable or disable the hover tooltip. Default: true.
- tooltip-format    : (string) Format of the text inside the tooltip.
- on-click          : (string) Command executed when left-clicking the module.
- on-click-middle   : (string) Command executed when middle-clicking the module.
- on-click-right    : (string) Command executed when right-clicking the module.
- on-scroll-up      : (string) Command executed when scrolling up over the module.
- on-scroll-down    : (string) Command executed when scrolling down over the module.
- interval          : (integer) Refresh interval in seconds for polling modules.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. SYSTEM PERFORMANCE MODULES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

[ cpu ]
Monitors overall CPU utilization.
- format            : Default is "{usage}%".
- format-icons      : (array) List of icons representing usage tiers.
- states            : (object) Threshold map defining CSS classes (e.g. "warning": 70).

[ memory ]
Monitors system RAM and swap usage.
- format            : Default "{percentage}%". Tokens: {used}, {total}, {avail}.
- states            : (object) Threshold map for styling alert states.

[ disk ]
Monitors disk space usage for a specified path.
- path              : (string) Mount point to monitor. Default is "/".
- format            : Default "{percentage_used}%". Tokens: {free}, {total}, {used}.

[ temperature ]
Monitors system hardware temperatures.
- thermal-zone      : (integer) The thermal zone index to track from ACPI.
- hwmon-path        : (string) Absolute path to a specific hwmon sysfs file instead.
- critical-threshold: (integer) Temperature value at which the 'critical' class applies.
- format            : Default "{temperatureC}°C".

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. HARDWARE & STATUS MODULES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

[ battery ]
Monitors battery status, capacity, and power states.
- bat               : (string) Specific battery device name (e.g., "BAT0").
- adapter           : (string) Specific AC adapter device name (e.g., "AC").
- full-at           : (integer) Define capacity threshold to consider "Full" (e.g. 98).
- format-charging   : (string) Format displayed when plugged in.
- format-discharging: (string) Format displayed on battery power.
- format-icons      : (array/object) Icons mapping to specific capacity percentages.

[ network ]
Monitors Wi-Fi and Ethernet connection states.
- interface         : (string) Specific network interface (e.g., "wlan0").
- format-wifi       : (string) Format when connected to Wi-Fi. (Tokens: {essid}, {signaldBm}).
- format-ethernet   : (string) Format when connected via cable. (Tokens: {ipaddr}, {cidr}).
- format-disconnected: (string) Format when offline.

[ backlight ]
Controls and displays monitor brightness levels.
- device            : (string) Specific backlight device name.
- format            : Default "{percent}%".
- on-scroll-up/down : Useful for adjusting brightness using brightnessctl or light.

[ wireplumber ] / [ pulseaudio ]
Monitors and manages system audio volume and mute state.
- format            : Default "{volume}%".
- format-muted      : Text/icon to show when muted.
- scroll-step       : (float) Percentage change per scroll tick.
- on-click          : Usually paired with tools like "pavucontrol" or volume muting toggles.

[ bluetooth ]
Monitors bluetooth adapter state and connected devices.
- format            : Display format when active.
- format-disabled   : Display format when disabled.
- format-connected  : Format when devices are paired (Tokens: {num_connections}, {device_alias}).
- on-click          : Usually mapped to a manager GUI like "blueman-manager".

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. ENVIRONMENT & ENVIRONMENT MANAGERS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

[ clock ]
Displays time, date, and calendar.
- format            : Standard strftime formatting (e.g., "{:%H:%M}").
- format-alt        : Format toggled when clicked.
- timezone          : (string) Force a specific timezone (e.g., "America/New_York").
- actions           : (object) Custom configurations for calendar scrolling/clicking.

[ idle_inhibitor ]
Toggles window manager idle state rules (inhibits screen lockers/sleep modes).
- format            : Structure using icons for active/inactive modes.
- format-icons      : (object) e.g., {"activated": "", "deactivated": ""}.

[ tray ]
Displays system tray icons for background applications.
- icon-size         : (integer) Defines the width/height of application tray icons.
- spacing           : (integer) Margin spacing between items inside the tray.
- show-passive-items: (bool) Whether to render passive tray applications.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. COMPOSITOR SPECIFIC MODULES (Hyprland / Sway)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

[ hyprland/workspaces ] / [ sway/workspaces ]
Monitors and controls workspace switching.
- format            : Format for workspace items. Supports token {name}.
- on-click          : Default action changes active workspace to the target clicked.
- all-outputs       : (bool) Show all workspaces across all monitors if true.
- format-icons      : (object) Map workspace designations/names to custom icons.

[ hyprland/window ] / [ sway/window ]
Displays the title of the currently focused window.
- format            : Default "{title}".
- max-length        : Highly recommended to avoid bar layout breaking on long titles.
- rewrite           : (object) Regex dictionary map to clean up long title names.

[ hyprland/submap ] / [ sway/mode ]
Displays current input submaps or binding configurations (e.g., resizing modes).
- format            : Default "{}" (outputs the mode name string).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. UTILITY & EXTENSION MODULES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

[ group ]
A container module that aggregates multiple modules into structural layouts.
- modules           : (array) List of children modules nested inside this group.
- orientation       : (string) Layout flow direction: "horizontal" or "vertical".
- drawer            : (object) Turns group into a collapsible panel.
    - transition-duration : (integer) Animation slide duration in milliseconds.
    - click-to-reveal    : (bool) Toggle drawer via click instead of hover.

[ custom/<name> ]
User-defined custom script runner module.
- exec              : (string) The terminal command or script path to run.
- exec-if           : (string) Guard command; script only runs if this exits with code 0.
- return-type       : (string) Expected stdout parsing mode: "json" or string.
- restart-interval  : (integer) Re-run interval loop if the script is not endless.
- signal            : (integer) POSIX signal tracking integer to trigger immediate refresh.
- escape            : (bool) Escape special XML/HTML markup tags from script output.
